PlanLiquidityTest
├── given the range sits below spot
│ ├── when the budget is token1-only
│ │ └── it mints without a swap and leaves the zap idle
│ └── when the budget is token0-only
│     └── it sells the whole budget down into the range and mints
├── given the budget exceeds the depth of the pool
│ ├── when the range is narrow
│ │ └── it still mints, pushing spot past the new range
│ ├── when the pool is thin
│ │ └── it still mints against the thin depth
│ └── when spot sits on the upper edge with a token0-only budget
│     └── it funds the whole mint from the reconcile sell
├── given spot lands exactly on a range boundary
│ ├── when the stored tick is below the boundary
│ │ └── it degenerates the in-range amount0 to 0 and mints
│ └── when the stored tick is at the boundary
│     └── it degenerates the in-range amount1 to 0 and mints
├── given an extreme tick
│ ├── when the budget is token0-only
│ │ └── it deploys at least 99.9% of the feasible liquidity
│ ├── when the budget is token1-only
│ │ └── it deploys at least 99.9% of the feasible liquidity
│ └── when the budget is two-sided at a tick far below 0
│     └── it values the token1 budget through the inverse rate
├── given the pool charges a protocol fee
│ └── it sizes from the swap fee of the direction, not the packed pair
├── given the pool hook overrides the LP fee
│ ├── it forwards hookData to beforeSwap and absorbs the difference in the trim
│ └── when minLiquidity is quoted at the stored fee
│     └── it reverts with {InsufficientLiquidity}
└── given any two-sided budget
    └── it mints and leaves the zap idle
